! mcp_bootstrap_p93.strap -- MCP, printed page 93: the tail of the
! TRACK ANALYSER, and LOCATE THE PROPER REEL SLOT FOR ENTRY.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.100, header "PAGE NUMBER 93".
!
! Forty-nine printed lines, thirty-four of which compile.  The page
! runs 005244.40 .. 005273.40 and is code throughout -- no SYN cards,
! no storage reservations.  Lines 1-3 and 31-33 box its two titles,
! and lines 9, 15, 21, 24, 27, 28, 37, 45 and 47 are the blank "-"
! separator lines the listing prints between blocks.
!
! >>> THE PAGE'S OWN TITLES ARE "TRACK ANALYSER" (line 2) AND
! "LOCATE THE PROPER REEL SLOT FOR ENTRY" (line 32). <<<  This page
! was taken as a continuation of the MOVE sub-routine that begins on
! printed p.88 at 005014.00; the address trail is continuous with it
! and every label here is a T-name, but the page prints no "MOVE"
! heading of its own.  Recorded as the page prints it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION TRAIL CLOSES ON ITSELF
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Thirteen rows compile a full word (4, 6, 7, 10, 11, 12, 13, 16,
! 18, 19, 22, 34, 48) and twenty-one compile a half word; walking the
! two lengths from 005244.40 reproduces every one of the thirty-
! four printed locations with nothing left over -- 13x64 + 21x32 =
! 1504 bits, and 005244.40 + 1504 bits is 005274.00.  Line 4 is a VFL
! word that STARTS AT A HALF-WORD BOUNDARY (005244.40 -> 005245.40),
! which is normal: instructions are addressed in half words.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> FOUR BRANCHES CHECK THE PAGE AGAINST ITSELF; FIVE DO NOT. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A branch half word prints as WWWWWW.OO HH, where the TOP BIT of
! the six-bit field (0o40) is the half-word selector.  Four branches
! on this page aim at labels DEFINED ON THIS PAGE, so their printed
! address is an independent check of both the decode rule and the
! label's own location:
!
!   line 35  BAE,TM6D     005266.76  -> 005266.40 = T M6D   (line 38)
!   line 36  BD,$         005266.04  -> 005266.00 = its own loc
!   line 40  CBZ,TMXGA,TOK 005262.66 -> 005262.40 = T OK    (line 25)
!   line 44  BZXVZ,TM6A   005270.71  -> 005270.40 = T M6A   (line 42)
!
! All four agree.  The other five branch targets are NOT on this
! page and are NOT in any deck transcribed so far -- T MDK1A and
! T MDK belong to printed p.92, T M6C, T MREJ and T N2 to printed
! p.94 and later.  Their values below are read off THIS page's
! binary column, so the rows that use them are self-referential and
! prove nothing about those five addresses; they are stand-ins, and
! the pages that declare them are the place to confirm them.  Two of
! them are at least double-attested HERE, which is why they are
! written as they are:
!
!   line 5  BRZ,TMDK1A  005242.34   and  line 8  B,TMDK1A  005242.10
!   line 17 BRZ,TMDK    005214.74   and  line 20 B,TMDK    005214.50
!
! -- two different ops, two different modifier patterns, the same
! word and the same half-word bit each time.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> LINE 35'S LAST GLYPH IS A D AND LINE 46'S IS A C, AND THEY
! LOOK ALIKE ON THE PAGE. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! At 400 dpi both lines read "TM6C".  They cannot be one symbol:
! line 35 compiles 005266.76 (= 005266.40) and line 46 compiles
! 005307.23 (= 005307.00).  Cropped to the same window at 1800 dpi
! and set beside the known-good D of line 38's own label, line 35's
! glyph has the D's STRAIGHT VERTICAL LEFT STEM and SQUARED top and
! bottom right corners with the middle of the bowl worn away, while
! line 46's is a round C with no stem at all -- the same arc as the
! C of line 4's "CT0011".  Ink and object code agree: line 35 is
! T M6D, line 46 is T M6C.  (Same hazard, same remedy, as printed
! p.87's "T WORM".)
!
! >>> AND THE SAME WORN D IS IN "T MDK", WHICH WAS TRANSCRIBED
! "T MCK" FIRST. <<<  Once line 35 proved the drum's D can print
! with its bowl worn through, EVERY C-or-D glyph on the page was
! re-rendered at 1800 dpi and set beside both a known-good D (line
! 38's label) and a known-good C (line 46's operand).  Six came
! back D:
!
!   line  4  T MDK2        line 10  T MNULD      line 29  T MDSK3
!   line  5  BRZ,TMDK1A    line  8  B,TMDK1A
!   line 17  BRZ,TMDK      line 20  B,TMDK
!
! The test is the LEFT side, not the right: this font's C and 0 are
! round with no stem (line 18's "CM0000(BU,3)", printed directly
! under line 17, has five of them in a row for comparison), while
! every glyph above has a straight vertical left stem and squared
! top and bottom right corners.  "B,TMDK" on line 20 prints its
! bowl closed and is the clearest of the six.
!
! The names read as a set that way, which is corroboration and not
! the reason: the TRACK ANALYSER's two arms are T MDK (disk, $R)
! and T MTRK (track, $L), beside T MNULD (null disk) and T MDSK3
! (illegal disk request).  NOTHING COMPILED CHANGES -- T MDK and
! T MDK1A are off-page stand-ins and T MDK2 is referenced nowhere
! on this page -- so the oracle cannot catch this one, and printed
! p.92, which defines T MDK and T MDK1A, is where it is settled
! for good.
!
! T OK (line 25) was checked the same way and is an O: the glyph
! is CLOSED on all four sides, unlike line 46's open C.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 4 IS "CT0011" AND NOT "C0011"
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Six characters, the second an unmistakable T, against line 48's
! five-character "C0011" on the same page in the same font.  The
! assembler settles it independently: CT0011(BU,3),$R+.61 compiles
! 000011.75 80  003000.07 70, which is the row exactly, while
! C0011(BU,3),$R+.61 compiles ...003000.06 70.  Connect for Test
! discards the result and sets indicators only, which is what the
! next line (BRZ) and the comment "CHECK FOR MULTIPLE OF 8" want.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TWO LISTING MARKS, AND ONE TRUNCATED COMMENT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 12 and 36 carry the bare "*" after their location that
! printed pp.3, 37, 38, 39 and 98 also carry.  It changes no
! compiled bit.
!
! Line 19's comment ends "...BEGINNING TRACK L".  THAT IS THE
! LISTING'S OWN TRUNCATION, not the crop: the right-edge render
! (x=5300..6700 at 400 dpi) shows the card-sequence numbers
! 18000554 etc. immediately to the right of it with clear paper
! between, so there is no more text to find.

        SLC, (8)5244.40

! ---- index names, printed p.83 lines 21-32 ------------------------
TMX1    SYN, $1
TMXD    SYN, $5
TMXG    SYN, $8
TMXEE   SYN, $9
TMXI    SYN, $10
TMXGA   SYN, $11
TMXH    SYN, TMX1
! ---- words and field offsets, printed pp.83, 84, 85 ---------------
TMMAX   SYN(BU,12), (8)4630.0        ! p.83 line 8, a DD(BU,12)
TMREEL  SYN(BU,24,6), (8)4630.44     ! p.83 line 10, (AX)DD(BU,24,6)
TIREF   SYN(BU,12), 0.52             ! p.84 line 25
TDSKRF  SYN(BU,12), 25.48            ! p.84 line 10
TIREEL  SYN(BU,48), 2.0              ! p.84 line 28
TFRLAD  SYN(BU,18), 8.0              ! p.84 line 51
TFMODE  SYN(BU,2), 2.48              ! p.85 line 11
TMXARC  SYN(BU,12), 5.38             ! p.85 line 13
! ---- STAND-INS, read off THIS page's binary column ----------------
! Not declared by any page transcribed so far.  See the note above:
! the rows that reference them carry no independent check.
TMDK1A  SYN, (8)5242.0               ! lines 5 and 8
TMDK    SYN, (8)5214.40              ! lines 17 and 20
TM6C    SYN, (8)5307.0               ! line 46
TMREJ   SYN, (8)5402.0               ! line 30
TN2     SYN, (8)5444.0               ! line 26

        SLC, (8)5244.40

! ---- TRACK ANALYSER (continued) -----------------------------------
TMDK2   CT0011(BU,3), $R+.61         ! line 4  -CHECK FOR MULTIPLE
                                      !           OF 8
        BRZ, TMDK1A                  ! line 5  -YES
        CM0000(BU,3), $R+.61         ! line 6  -ZERO THE TRIVIAL BITS
        M+1(BU,9), $R+.52            ! line 7  -ADD NEXT BEGINNING
                                      !           TRACK LOC
        B, TMDK1A                    ! line 8
TMNULD  LF, TIREF(TMXI)              ! line 10 -IF NULL DISK OR
                                      !           TRACK ,GET REF NO.
        ST, TDSKRF(TMXG)             ! line 11
        LF, TMMAX                    ! line 12 -GET THE MAX DISK
                                      !           NUMBER POSSIBLE  (*)
        ST, TMXARC(TMXD)             ! line 13
        B, TM1FA                     ! line 14
TMTRK   CT0011(BU,3), $L+.61         ! line 16 -CHECK FOR MULTIPLE
                                      !           OF 8
        BRZ, TMDK                    ! line 17 -YES - RETURN
        CM0000(BU,3), $L+.61         ! line 18 -NO ZERO THE TRIVIAL
                                      !           BITS
        M+1(BU,9), $L+.52            ! line 19 -ADD ON TO GET NEXT
                                      !           BEGINNING TRACK L
        B, TMDK                      ! line 20
        CM1111(BU,1), TFMODE+.1(TMXD) ! line 22 -A DUMMY ONE FOR
                                      !           ALL BUT TAPE
TM1FA   V+I, TMXD, 7.0               ! line 23 -STEP THE VF BY A
                                      !           FILE TABLE
TOK     LVI, TMX1, 0.0               ! line 25 -OK RETURN
        B, TN2                       ! line 26
TMDSK3  LVI, TMX1, 1.0               ! line 29 -ILLEGAL DISK REQ
        B, TMREJ                     ! line 30 -GO TO REJECT JOB

! ---- LOCATE THE PROPER REEL SLOT FOR ENTRY ------------------------
TM6     KF, TMREEL                   ! line 34 -CHECK FOR A REEL CARD
        BAE, TM6D                    ! line 35 -OK
        BD, $                        ! line 36 -MCP ERROR, INVALID
                                      !           OP CODE ON CD.  (*)
TM6D    LV, TMXG, TFRLAD(TMXEE)      ! line 38 -GET INITIAL REEL ENTRY
        LX, TMXGA, 0.0(TMXI)         ! line 39 -TO GET THE REEL COUNT
        CBZ, TMXGA, TOK              ! line 40 -GET 1ST REEL LOC IF ANY
        LV, TMXGA, TMXI              ! line 41 -GET FIRST REEL ADDRESS
TM6A    LV, TMXH, TMXG               ! line 42 -SAVE FOR LAST ENTRY
        LX, TMXG, 0.0(TMXG)          ! line 43 -LOOK AHEAD ONE SLOT
        BZXVZ, TM6A                  ! line 44 -IF THERE IS AN ENTRY
        BXF, TM6C                    ! line 46 -IF A REEL NUMBER IS
                                      !           ENTERED
TN6     C0011, TIREEL(TMXGA)         ! line 48 -GET A REEL NAME FROM
                                      !           BREAKDOWN
        Z, 0.0(TMXH)                 ! line 49 -CLEAR THE REEL SLOT
                                      !           FIRST

